 "notes": "Observed 95% one-sided upper limit on g_agamma from ABRACADABRA-10cm Run 3 (broadband), traced from the vector paths of Fig. 4 (Plots/Joint_Limit.pdf in the e-print), black '95% U.L. [This Work]' curve, not the expected 1/2-sigma bands or Run 1 curve. Axes calibrated from tick-mark coordinates (x: 0.3-8 neV log; y: 1e-10, 1e-9 GeV^-1 log); calibration cross-checked against the stated mass range 0.41-8.27 neV (100 kHz-2 MHz plot edges). Curve resampled to 100 log-spaced points via bin-median of ~10k path vertices. Per the caption the plotted curve is smoothed over the ~11.1 million analyzed mass points; the strongest unsmoothed limit is 3.2e-11 GeV^-1 at m_a ~ 2.99 neV, while the smoothed curve reaches ~6.6e-11 GeV^-1 near 3 neV. Assumes axion is all of local DM with rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 and Standard Halo Model (v0=220 km/s, vsun=232 km/s).",
